                  "props": {
                    "markdown": "The failure reproduces: 375 vs 1125. Per the card workflow, a writer makes the change in its own worktree.\n\nI ran the API tests: 2 pass and 1 fails. \"cart total counts each line's quantity\" expects 1125 and gets 375, because `cartTotal` in `api/src/cart.ts` adds `line.price` once per line instead of `line.price * line.quantity`.\n\nA writer subagent is making that one-line change in its own worktree and committing it there, without touching the tests. It's still running. When it returns, I'll merge its branch into `card/2-the-cart-total-ignores-quantity`, run `npm test` again on the card branch, and report the result.\n\nMerged and green; now cleaning up the writer's worktree and branch.\n\nCart totals now count quantity, and the API's tests pass. `cartTotal` in `api/src/cart.ts` multiplies each line's price by its quantity before adding VAT.\n\n- **Before:** 2 pass, 1 fail. \"cart total counts each line's quantity\" got 375 instead of 1125.\n- **After:** 3 pass, 0 fail, 1 skipped (\"currency rounding per market\" was already skipped).\n\nThe fix (commit 2a23e58) is merged into `card/2-the-cart-total-ignores-quantity`. I didn't change any tests, and nothing is pushed.\n\nOne cleanup step failed. I removed the writer's worktree folder, but the sandbox wouldn't let me delete git's own record of that worktree (`.git/worktrees/agent-af9c71177cb18213e`). Git won't delete the merged branch `worktree-agent-af9c71177cb18213e` while that record exists. To finish the cleanup, run:\n\n```\n! git worktree prune && git branch -d worktree-agent-af9c71177cb18213e\n```"
                  }
                }
              ]
